WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:46.220
Cardinal Garnest Hogue.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.420
Lord Galil...

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.960
Thou hast been informed of what 
transpired in Taurus, I assume?

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.100
Yes, lord...

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.890
I shall leave the cleanup to thee.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.520
Under no circumstances must rumors 
of people defying Providence

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.140
be allowed to promulgate 
among the lower classes.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.980
May the will of Mauser be done...

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.230
I am told that the kingdom 
has placed a bounty

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.360
upon the head of the 
Scrapped Princess, as well.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.690
Yes. Nevertheless,

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:19.320
I expect that I shall have to 
take personal action next time.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:24.330
"Lullaby of the Troubadour"

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.410
Would you please slow down?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.590
Please, tell me what 
happened back in the city!

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:36.500
Oh, you intend to treat me 
as an outsider, don't you?!

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.800
Oh, you were an insider, Leo?

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.260
M-Miss Raquel... That was cruel...

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.420
I guess we'll have to say goodbye 
to Leo sooner than we thought.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.990
What a pretty song...

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.120
He must be a troubadour.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.610
Hello, there, everyone.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.080
Would you care for a song to 
comfort you on your journey?

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.210
A song of joy to pluck up your spirits?

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.840
Or a sad tune to call forth tears?

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.580
It is all up to your personal tastes.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.050
Oh, my fetching blonde lass!

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.130
How I wish to sing songs of 
love in your lovely ears.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.440
If you put it that way, maybe 
I wouldn't mind hearing them...

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.440
I'll just bet, I'll just bet!

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.400
You can pay me later.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.280
But first, let's start with a line 
from an ancient tune of sad love...

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.910
No thanks. Try somewhere else.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.540
Now, now, don't say such things.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.870
What I'm saying is, get lost.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.340
Hey, Shannon! What brought this on?!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.840
We're in a hurry, so if you'll excuse us...

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.980
Oh, I see. That's too bad!

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.410
I shouldn't keep you, then.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.590
Well, if we meet again somewhere, 
I'll hope we can do business, okay?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.900
You think he was...

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.570
Probably.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.860
The instant he came close, 
he tried to attack.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.490
He didn't look like a wizard.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.370
He wasn't carrying anything that 
looked like a weapon, either.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.580
That's why he was suspicious.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.450
What a foppish fellow he was.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.490
If he comes near us again,

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.420
I'll drive him off!

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.860
A frontal attack won't work, huh?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.050
These people are pretty tough.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:46.970
Enter.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.850
I apologize that I was unable to 
attend the commander's funeral.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.100
That's all right.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.320
Still, this is most unusual.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.690
Failure isn't tolerated 
in the Special Forces.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.280
You understand that, I assume?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.110
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.800
I am prepared to accept whatever 
punishment you see fit.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.830
The new commander of the Special Forces 
hasn't assigned you a punishment,

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.670
but rather a new mission.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.130
New commander?

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.050
You, ma'am?

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:25.350
I want you to reopen an investigation.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:30.470
Regarding the Grendel Revelation fifteen 
years ago and the Scrapped Princess.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.940
This is so good!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.000
Omelets are the best!

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.240
Don't eat too much.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.400
You'll make the cart too heavy.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:47.200
Oh, shut up! I'm a growing girl.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.370
I guess you're more about 
food appeal than sex appeal.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:53.220
No, Miss Pacifica has sex appeal, all right!

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.370
Please be careful around foppish men 
like that one from earlier today!

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.080
Is that jealousy I hear?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.380
I-It's nothing of the sort!

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.460
Men who act overly familiar when 
they've just met you are dangerous.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.610
I seem to recall someone 
proposing when we first met...

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:12.660
I'm done! I'll go wash the dishes.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.100
Wait a moment! I'll assist you!

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.350
Miss Pacifica!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.940
Geez, those two are so noisy...

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.860
Just in case, I'll make sure that 
no one suspicious is in the area.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.250
Hm?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.130
What is it?

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.850
This signal...

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:45.840
It's like the troubadour from earlier.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.200
Is he off in the direction Pacifica went?

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.970
Actually, he's in the completely 
opposite direction.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.110
I thought I told you to get lost.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:04.690
Oh, I heard you, all right.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.810
But I have a trade to ply.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.910
You certainly have a short fuse.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.370
You're not a Royal Forces soldier.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:18.500
I guess that makes that busted 
instrument your weapon.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.830
It's not broken.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.830
It's making sounds just fine.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.790
Human ears can't hear it, that's all.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:25.900
What the...?

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.190
Bugs?

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.140
You'll die if you're stung, so be careful.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:44.430
I've heard about a clan of 
assassins who control Bugs.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.690
I thought it was just a rumor.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.150
These are mysterious creatures,

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.160
so it takes a great deal 
of skill to control them.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:59.540
I'm Keydarf Gylot, master 
of the silent melody.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.620
My nickname is The Silencer.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.580
Nice to meet you.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.540
Are you sure you should be 
over here quarreling with me?

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.130
What?

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.590
One of these fellows' brothers

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:16.760
should be reaching the Scrapped 
Princess right about now.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.520
C'mon, Leo, are you done yet?

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.320
Just a moment, Miss Pacifica.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:23.580
This bit of dirt is rather stubborn.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:38.660
Are you all right?

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:42.960
That hurt! What the heck was that?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:47.990
Pacifica!

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.450
I was there with her, and yet...

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.050
I'm not fit to be a knight!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.480
I think she's getting worse.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.890
She must need an antidote.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:08.730
Let's go back to Taurus and get a doctor.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.320
I'm not so sure.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.780
I don't know if the townspeople 
will do us any favors.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.530
Shannon! Miss Raquel!

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:22.160
I'll go visit Doyle Barrett!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.250
Doyle?

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.500
That former knight?

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.460
Sir Barrett also works as a doctor.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.590
I think I should go to him and 
ask him to help Miss Pacifica.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.800
You're right... That old man might...

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.800
If we take the highway,

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.010
we can make it there and back in half a day.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.430
Very well, I'll hurry back!

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.040
Wait, I'm coming with you.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.500
No, I will.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.020
Raquel?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.090
You're terrible at asking 
for help, remember?

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.690
Stay with her.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.230
Baroness? What is this uniform for?

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.700
It looks wonderful on a 
handsome boy such as yourself.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.370
I can't go to Castle Sauer dressed like this.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.120
I'll stick out like a sore thumb.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.790
Not at all, Christopher Bairach.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.130
I've pulled some strings with the registrar.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.280
Starting today, you are my adopted child,

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.270
the heir of House Bairach.

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:16.010
Baroness!

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.360
"Mother," don't you mean?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:23.750
A title will prove useful during 
the investigation I mentioned.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.680
I understand, Mother.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:33.570
Your Highness Prince 
Forsyth, a fine day to you.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.650
And to you, Baroness.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.950
This is Christopher, my foster son.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.870
He was raised in the provinces,

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.170
but I would be delighted if you 
would offer him your friendship.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:49.410
It would be my honor. I am pleased 
to meet you, Christopher.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.600
You honor me, Highness.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.790
Please, would you call me Forsyth?

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.340
Of course, Prince Forsyth.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.590
Do you know much about the provinces?

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.800
Yes, a little.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.520
Tell me, Christopher.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.850
Have you heard this rumor?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.310
The rumor that says that the 
Scrapped Princess is alive?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:13.520
Come now, does an august 
personage such as yourself

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.320
truly believe in such 
nonsense, Prince Forsyth?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.280
When the Royal Wizard 
attended my aunt's funeral,

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:27.950
he apparently spotted a blonde 
girl with blue eyes there.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.050
In a little town called Manurhin.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:36.180
My twin sister, who was scrapped 
right after her birth...

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:42.720
She may be alive somewhere 
in this wide world.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.310
Leo, go faster!

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:57.020
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.580
Didn't I tell you that I'd 
given up being a knight?

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:11.910
You misunderstand!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:13.500
We need your help as a doctor.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.420
Bugs, huh? That's tricky.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.840
Is this an insect?

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.630
They say they're creatures 
that were created by demons.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.130
But I don't know much about them,

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.600
except that they're extremely dangerous.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.930
If you're directly stung 
by them, you die instantly.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.940
If you're even grazed by it,

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.020
you probably won't live to see the next dawn.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.230
You can't be serious!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.610
Please, save my sister.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:39.820
I beg of you.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.480
Even if I wanted to,

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.950
normal antidotes don't work on Bug poison.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:48.070
You need to mix up some wild medicinal herbs.

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:50.910
Plus, they only grow in special locations.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:52.370
Where are they?

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.710
The only area around here is inside a 
strange cave that's called the Fortress.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:58.500
The Fortress?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.340
Let's go there at once!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.380
There's a Bug hive inside.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.590
Without a military wizard, 
we'd never come out alive.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.940
In that case, I'll go.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:11.100
What?! Miss Raquel, you can use magic?!

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:12.310
Yes, a little.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.980
That's the Fortress?

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.740
Was this made by humans?

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.930
They say it's a relic of the Genesis Wars.

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.040
That it was some kind of vehicle.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.620
Nobody knows for sure, though.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.140
Let's go.

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:42.670
I'll protect you!

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.040
You're an impressive woman.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:50.140
You think so?

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:51.930
Even for a military wizard,

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:53.850
this place is dangerous if 
you let your guard down.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.060
My sister's life is on the line.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:01.570
Shannon...

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.990
You're awake, huh?

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.780
I... What happened to me?

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.460
You probably found something 
weird on the ground and ate it.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.000
Leo and Raquel went out to get medicine,

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.010
so you'll be fine when you take it.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:18.800
Shannon...

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.650
Whenever you lie, you cover your mouth.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:23.380
You always do that.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.210
Oh, shut up.

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:26.770
If this keeps up, and I...

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:29.610
If I die,

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:35.890
you and Raquel will be able 
to go back to Manurhin, right?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:36.730
I guess.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.150
Now nobody has to die...

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.440
Everybody dies. Eventually.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:47.400
I think something every once in a while...

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:51.570
That if everyone would be better 
off without me, maybe I should...

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.370
Shut up! Be quiet and sleep!

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.830
What's with this "if I die" crap?

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.040
Give this whole "thinking of others 
and being a good person" thing a rest!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.000
Don't try to take the easy way out!

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:07.140
Just this once, sit back and let 
other people fawn over you, okay?

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:09.570
Big brother...

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:10.970
What?

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.680
Hold my hand...

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:27.110
Why do you suppose the walls glow like this?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:33.160
Tradition has it that this place is 
under the curse of Dark Lord Browning.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:39.200
Who taught you that sword style?

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.060
No one, sir. It's my own style.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:44.290
Your swing is stiff, but it's quick.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:46.250
Thank you, sir!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.500
It's an honor to be complimented by you!

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.010
All I did was give you my impression.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.900
Um, Sir Barrett?

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:55.640
I realize this isn't the best time...

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:56.720
What?

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.900
Well, was throwing the Scrapped 
Princess into the gorge

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:03.270
really the cause of your 
quitting the knighthood?

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.980
That old woman should have 
minded her own business...

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:09.940
But wasn't that also a knight's duty?

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.380
He wields his sword in the name of justice,

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:15.620
and if need be, takes lives.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.410
And if many lives would be 
saved by that act, then...

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:20.700
No matter how great the cause,

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.160
it's no excuse to take away 
the innocent smile of a child.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.070
But...

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:25.290
That's enough!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.630
Drop the topic.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.770
Even so...

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.690
Don't you think that there haven't 
been very many Bug attacks?

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:34.590
Now that you mention it...

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:40.400
Welcome to my charming palace.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.730
You're the man from this morning!

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.140
One of them didn't return,

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:49.190
so I thought this might happen...

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:52.530
The little lady is still alive, isn't she?

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.160
Yes. We came here to get medicinal herbs.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:57.740
If it's herbs you're after, there's plenty.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:00.410
But will you be able to pick them?

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:05.330
People of the flames, dance!

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:11.710
Amazing!

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:13.720
I suspected as much.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.680
How about <i>this</i>, then?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:20.260
I'm sorry,

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:23.430
but I'm going to help myself to 
that bounty of 5 million cetme.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.440
Bounty? What are you talking about?

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:27.900
Oh, you don't know?

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:31.150
Oh, 'tis a strange and terrible tale!

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:35.120
A suckling child who was the 
subject of a revelation.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:38.530
The poisonous, lovely young girl 
who would usher in destruction.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:43.080
In other words, the Scrapped Princess 
that the kingdom failed to exterminate...

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.920
is that young lady.

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.040
She's what?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.000
If you think I'm lying, ask the lady there.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.750
It can't be...

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.480
Is this true?

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:57.720
It's true.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.060
No matter what it says in the revelation,

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.470
she's my precious little sister.

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:06.980
Miss Pacifica is the Scrapped Princess?

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:08.730
She's alive?

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:11.150
Which means that if I kill Pacifica,

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.940
I'll be able to collect a huge 
amount of money from the king.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.700
Barrier, protect us!

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.580
A defensive spell, huh?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.790
How long can you keep it up?

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.890
Damn it... Why did I fall 
for a trap like that?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:52.020
I swore that I'd protect her, 
no matter what, didn't I?

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:54.860
Pacifica...

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.990
If you're going to pick the medicinal herbs,

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:04.530
you'll have to take down 
that defensive spell.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.980
Will you give up and go home,

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.000
or will you die here?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.420
Either way, the Scrapped Princess will be...

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:14.340
I hate to take lives for no reason, but...

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:34.310
I can alter the size and shape of 
the spell's barrier as required.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:36.260
What?!

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:37.780
Now, then, Silencer.

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:40.170
Will you die like this,

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:44.740
or will you call off your 
Bugs and hand over the herbs?

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.720
You're joking, right?

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.330
Are you really capable of killing someone?

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.130
Death it is, then.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:59.940
W-Wait! Wait a minute! I give, I give!

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:29.900
The young plants are no good.

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:32.000
Pick the thick, green ones.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:35.360
Right!s

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:41.140
We don't have much time!

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:42.420
Make the horse go faster!

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.470
I know, I know!

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.390
The Scrapped Princess...

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:56.210
Miss Pacifica is the poison 
that will destroy the world.

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:46.510
"Next Time"

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:37.040
Doyle drives his horse hard to save Pacifica.

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:40.720
And Leo, having found out that she is 
the Scrapped Princess, is at a loss.

00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:45.510
But just then, an unimaginable 
power begins to stir around them.

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:47.350
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:47.350 --> 00:22:49.180
"The Pied Piper Song of the Knights."

00:22:49.180 --> 00:22:50.510
Please tune in!
